      "rule": "R19",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The law assumes that `ok` implies database-wide constraint atoms for every supported form, but SQLite 3.51.0 returns `ok` for `integrity_check(good)` and `quick_check(good)` when another table violates CHECK, as [partial checks inspect only the named table](https://www.sqlite.org/pragma.html#pragma_integrity_check). Fix: use database atoms for whole-database checks and the named table’s atoms for table-specific checks."
